  "english": "...Creator of all things. Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [g-k]: Vision of the Lightning-like (Tesil paylaknadzev).\n\n24. Monday. Tone 7 [d-dz]. Saints Cyricus and Julitta, \nand Gordius, Polyeuctus, and \nGrigoris. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 2 [a-k]: You who are exalted (Or bardsratsyalt es).\n\n25. Tuesday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Saint Vahan of Goghtn, \nand Eugenia the virgin, and others. \nPatristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 3 [b-dz]: Without malice (Anokhakal).\n\n27. Thursday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Eugenius, Macarius, \nand others. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 3 [b-dz]: With your saints (End sourbs ko).\n\n29. Saturday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Gregory the Theologian.\n\n30. Sunday. Tone 5 [g-dz]. Third [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 6 [g-k]: Today the uncreated (Aysor zenaun). Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [g-dz]: In the awesome voice (I dzayn ahegh).\n\n31. Monday. Tone 6 [g-k]. The Maccabees, Eleazar, \nand others. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [b-k]: We bless you, Lord (Orhnemk zkhez ter).\n\nFebruary\n\n1. Tuesday. Tone 7 [d-dz]. The Twelve Prophets: \nHosea, and others.\n\n3. Thursday. Tone 2 [a-z / a-dz]. Sophia and her three daughters. \nPatristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [b-k]: Who in the battle (Ork i marti).\n\n5. Saturday. Tone 3 [b-dz]. Sons and grandsons of the \nIlluminator.\n\n6. Sunday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Fourth [Sunday]. Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [b-k]: The Resurrection of Christ (Zyarutiun Kristosi). Eve of the \nFast of Catechumens [Arachavorats].\n\n7. Monday. Tone 5 [g-dz]. Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats]. Penitential \nPatristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [b-k]: Lord God of our fathers (Ter astvads hartsn).\n\n13. Sunday. Tone 7 [d-dz]. Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [b-dz]: The wondrous women (Skancheli kanaykn).\n\n14. Monday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnendarach].\n\n15. Tuesday. Tone 5 [g-dz]. The Atomian saints and the \nSukiasian saints. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 6 [g-k]: Heavenly hosts (Zinvorutiunk).\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Great Lent [Bun Barekendan]. See \nthe others according to the order in the First Volume, up to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping \nthe local order.\n\nApril\n\n7. Thursday. Tone 7 [d-dz]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy \nVirgin.\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection of \nChrist our God. See \naccording to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMay\n\nThursday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Ascension of Christ. \nAnd the rest according to the order.\n\nJune\n\nSunday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. \nEve of the Elijah Fast.\n\nSunday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the \nSundays of the Resurrection. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 1 [a-dz]: Who came for salvation (Or ekir i prkutiun).\n\nJuly\n\nSunday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Sixth [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 3 [b-dz]: Who descended from heaven (Or i yerknits ijer). Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [b-k]: Your Resurrection (Ko yarutiand). Eve of the \nFast of Transfiguration [Vardavar].\n\nSunday. Tone 3 [b-dz]. Transfiguration [Vardavar]. The abstinence-free period [utikh] \nis two weeks. See the First Volume \nup to the Friday of the second week, and on Saturday come back here; \nbut look here for the Sunday Patristic Hymns.\n\nSunday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Second [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [b-k]: Who with the heavenly hosts (Or yerknayin zinvoru). Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [a-k]: You were sent from the Father (Araketsar i hore).\n\nAugust\n\nSaturday. Tone 8 [d-k]. The Holy Council of Ephesus of the \ntwo hundred Patriarchs.\n\nSunday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. Third [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 5 [g-dz]: We glorify \nyou (Paravoremk zkhez). Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [a-dz]: Glory \nto the Resurrection (Park yarutian). Eve of the Fast of the Holy \nMother of God [Astvadsatsin].\n\nMonday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. \nPatristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 2 [a-k]: Ineffable Essence (Zanchar eutyun).\n\nSunday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Assumption [Verapokhumn] of the Holy \nMother of God. The abstinence-free period [utikh] is three \nweeks. See the First Volume, \nkeeping the local order.\n\nSeptember\n\nSunday. Tone 5 [g-dz]. Fourth [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 6 [g-k]: Ineffable (Anchareli). Evening Resurrection Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [g-dz]: The Myrrh-bearing women (Yughaber), and \nToday the Resurrection (Aysor yarutiun). Eve of the \nFast of the Holy Cross.",
